-# Stage 8 — PNX journal/block-state adapter
+# Stage 9 — transactional placement to durable journal bridge
 
 Target PNX commit: `c57499365737654eca32df008751ef6bca5af142`.
 
-This stage adds the first adapter that understands actual PNX `BlockState`, `Level`, `IChunk`, and `BlockManager` APIs.
+This stage adds a platform-neutral transaction coordinator that turns nested Terra placement scopes into one durable write-ahead-journal frame per root placement.
 
-## Included
+## Semantics
 
-- `PnxBlockStatePayloadCodec`: durable payload is `(format magic, version, block identifier, specialValue)`. It deliberately does not persist `blockStateHash`, because that is an internal registry hash. Decode resolves the state through `Registries.BLOCK` and rejects unknown/noncanonical states.
-- `PnxJournalChunkApplier`: reads journal operations for one target chunk, resolves deterministic winners per coordinate+layer, applies them through PNX `BlockManager`, and refuses to load missing chunks. `REPLACEABLE_ONLY` is evaluated against the pre-apply block through an injected predicate.
-- Per-target asynchronous serialization and repeat-until-stable behavior. A later journal append invalidates the digest and triggers another pass.
-- Durable acknowledgement is written only after an injected chunk persistence future succeeds. Failure leaves the ledger unacknowledged and safe to replay.
+- Root scope owns the stable `PlacementKey`, priority, and conflict policy.
+- Nested Terra structure scopes are savepoints. Their descriptor may differ, but they inherit the root identity and policy.
+- Nested commit merges writes into its parent only; it never appends independently.
+- Nested abort discards only that savepoint's writes.
+- Root abort discards the entire placement.
+- Root commit encodes all staged block states first, then appends one complete placement frame through `CrossChunkPlacementJournal.append()`.
+- Encoding or WAL failure leaves the root scope open, so the caller can retry or explicitly abort. No partial journal frame is published by the coordinator.
+- Each committed write receives a deterministic ordinal based on the root placement's write order; the journal rejects duplicate ordinals.
+- Scopes are thread-confined and must close in LIFO order.
 
-## Exact PNX source observations
+## API integration point
 
-- `Level.getChunkIfLoaded(int,int)` exists and does not request generation.
-- `IChunk` exposes `getBlockState`, `isGenerated`, `isInitiated`, and dimension height.
-- `BlockManager.setBlockStateAt(x,y,z,layer,state)` and `applySubChunkUpdate()` provide the platform write path, including block-entity holder creation and chunk dirty marking.
-- `BlockProperties.getBlockState(short)` and `containBlockState(BlockState)` allow registry-validated identifier/special-value payloads.
+`PlacementTransactionCoordinator<S>` accepts a `StateEncoder<S>`. In PNX-Terra, instantiate it with `PnxBlockStatePayloadCodec::encode` and stage the actual `org.powernukkitx.block.BlockState` from `PNXServerWorld.setBlockState()` in the active scope. The Terra `PlacementScopeProvider` adapter must derive the root `PlacementKey` from the root `PlacementDescriptor` plus world seed/dimension and pass nested descriptors through `begin()`; nested descriptors are intentionally mapped to the inherited root identity.
 
-## Important integration boundary
+The PNX adapter must still preserve the current transactional read overlay for `getBlockState()` and must route both block layers through the same root transaction. This stage does not silently replace or modify the existing `PNXServerWorld` implementation.
 
-The adapter intentionally does not invent a `LevelProvider` persistence call. The PNX integration must supply `ChunkPersister` using the pinned provider's actual save contract. The caller must also keep the target chunk non-publishable until this future completes and the digest is acknowledged. Do not mark the ledger before persistence.
+## Validation
 
-This is not yet a complete PNX/Terra runtime integration. It does not patch `Level.generateChunk`, does not install a concrete generation-stage driver, and does not gate all packet publication paths. It is the PNX-facing journal application layer required before those hooks can safely be wired.
+Standalone core compiled with `javac --release 21 -Xlint:all -Werror`.
+
+Passed:
+- journal durability, duplicate identity, conflict selection, negative chunk coordinates, torn-tail recovery;
+- dependency bounds/barriers and late digest invalidation;
+- generation request coalescing/retry;
+- dependency scheduler failure propagation;
+- nested savepoint commit and abort isolation;
+- atomic cross-chunk root publication;
+- root identity inheritance for nested descriptors;
+- encoder failure leaves scope open and publishes no operations;
+- WAL recovery of cross-chunk placement.
+
+## Not yet complete
+
+- No concrete `PNXServerWorld` wiring yet; this is the tested transaction bridge core.
+- No exact descriptor-to-key adapter (world seed, dimension ID, rotation encoding and root path must be bound in the PNX-Terra integration).
+- No PNX/Terra Gradle build or runtime test.
+- No concrete chunk persister or publication gate; these remain separate integration work.
+- No entity or block-entity transaction journal.
+- No production server files, world data, player data, configuration, plugins, or JARs were modified.
